{
  "info": {
    "name": "ZATCA API (ERPNext)",
    "_postman_id": "b7f1c2d4-5e6a-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e",
    "description": "# ZATCA API\n\nREST bridge for creating ERPNext Sales Invoices from an external system and getting the **ZATCA QR code** back in the same response.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Open the **ZATCA API** environment and fill in `base_url`, `api_key`, `api_secret`, `company`, `customer`, `item_code`.\n2. Generate the key pair in ERPNext: **User > (your API user) > Settings > API Access > Generate Keys**. The secret is shown once.\n3. Run **01 Ping** first. It reports whether authentication works, whether the custom fields are migrated, and which ZATCA phase each company resolves to.\n4. Then run the requests in order - later ones reuse `last_invoice` and `external_id` captured by earlier ones.\n\n## Response shape\n\nFrappe wraps every whitelisted return value in `message`, so the envelope is at `message`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": {\n    \"success\": true,\n    \"request_id\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f6\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-08-04 11:30:00\",\n    \"data\": { \"invoice\": { ... }, \"zatca\": { ... } },\n    \"warnings\": [],\n    \"errors\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe shape is identical for success and failure, so one parser handles both.\n\n## The zatca block\n\n`data.zatca` is **always present**. Check `available`:\n\n| Field | Phase 1 | Phase 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `phase` | `Phase 1` | `Phase 2` |\n| `qr_content` | null (helper returns an image only) | base64 TLV string |\n| `qr_format` | `png-only` | `base64-tlv` |\n| `qr_png_base64` | yes | yes |\n| `uuid` / `invoice_hash` | null (no filing) | yes |\n| `integration_status` | `Not Applicable` | ZATCA outcome, asynchronous |\n\nWhen `available` is false, `reason` says why - most often the invoice is still in Draft, or the company has no ZATCA settings.\n\n## Timing\n\nThe UUID, invoice hash, PIH and QR are computed **locally at submission** and are in the create response immediately. Only `integration_status` moves asynchronously, because the clearance/reporting call to ZATCA runs in a background job. Poll **10 Get ZATCA status** for it.\n\n## HTTP status codes\n\n`200` ok - `400` validation_error - `401` unauthorized - `403` forbidden (also returned for a wrong HTTP verb) - `404` not_found - `409` duplicate / immutable_document - `424` zatca_unavailable - `502` upstream_error - `503` app_disabled - `500` internal_error\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
