        "description": "Everything a ZATCA Phase 2 STANDARD (B2B) invoice needs.\n\nKey points:\n- `tax_id` is mirrored onto Customer.custom_vat_registration_number, which is the field ksa_compliance reads to decide standard vs simplified. Sending only a bare tax_id elsewhere would file a B2B sale as simplified.\n- `address_parts` supplies the buyer street, building number (4 digits), district, city and postal code (5 digits) that ZATCA requires. Missing parts come back in `warnings`.\n- `item_tax_template` per line keeps mixed standard/zero-rated/exempt lines correct.\n- Set {{item_tax_template}} and {{vat_account}} in the environment, or delete those keys.",
